Overdesk shares one keyboard and mouse across your Mac, Windows PC, Linux and
BSD machines: move the pointer off the edge of one screen and it arrives on
the next. The clipboard and files follow. Connections are mutual TLS 1.3
between paired devices; nothing goes through a server.

This is the open core. It runs on X11, and on Wayland sessions that offer the
xdg-desktop-portal InputCapture and RemoteDesktop interfaces (for example
KDE Plasma 6.1 or newer).
